    <string name="install_permission_title">Install unknown apps is off</string>
    <string name="install_permission_body">Android reports that this app may not install packages. On this head unit that answer is sometimes wrong: the system installer still opens. Open the settings page and grant it, or continue and let the installer ask.\n\nThe state is re-checked before every install because this platform drops some app permissions across reboots.</string>
    <string name="install_permission_open">Open settings</string>
    <string name="install_permission_anyway">Continue anyway</string>

    <string name="disclaimer_title">Read this first</string>
    <string name="disclaimer_body">Experimental, unofficial software. Not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by ZEEKR. Not certified for any vehicle safety function. Do not operate this app while driving.\n\nIt exists because a firmware update closed the door on fresh installs. Keeping this app installed, signed with the same key, is the only way new code can still arrive. Uninstalling returns the head unit to its factory apps; there is no door back in.\n\nIt holds no root, no system writes, and no wake locks.</string>
    <string name="disclaimer_accept">I understand</string>

